# pool_attacked: host
# object_attacked: heap:torch:torch.int64 held_by=dict
#
# object     published table's name; rank 1 at s4's peak, 961,500 kB (42.0%). Owner census: 950.2 of
#            961.5 MB (98.8%) embedding-shaped:
#              534.5 MB  n=3   (28996, 768)      the embedding table
#              237.5 MB  n=8   (1, 128, 28996)   the one-hot intermediates
#              178.2 MB  n=1   (22268928,)       28996 x 768 flat
# cost_class: paid
# evidence: equivalent
# plaintext_equivalence: impl/equiv_embed_chunk.py
#
# phase B    (a) transcript on these runs:
#                  s4_onnx_and_spill   TRANSCRIPT|bytes=11228688384|rounds=1495
#                  s5_embed_chunk      TRANSCRIPT|bytes=11228688384|rounds=1525
#                same bytes, +30 rounds (SHAFT-GPU 1496 -> 1526). Counter-example: BumbleBee
#                x7_nonlinear_chunk, -28.9% with passing gate, retracted for +41% bytes.
#            (b) impl/equiv_embed_chunk.py against this port: six cases bit-identical over int64
#                (measured configuration, non-dividing chunk count, more chunks than entries, one-chunk
#                no-op, wraparound).
# gate       sixteen Beaver triples, sixteen mask streams: worst relative difference 1.517e-02 vs 1e-06
#            tolerance (a different mask stream moves the observable 2.34 on 0.135; here 0.002).
# cost       paid: wall 100.6 s vs s4's 98.1 s (+2.6%; own spread 0.875%, predecessor's 2.574%); thirty
#            extra rounds, no extra bytes. Free levers exhausted (all 21 modules measured;
#            graph_clear_values_cpu 0.02% twice on 17.08.).
#
# s5_embed_chunk: private embedding one-hot matmul in 16 vocabulary chunks.
#
# table      p_census_owner_s4 (rss 2,332,684 vs peak 2,336,656 kB, 0.17%; deduplicated by data_ptr):
#              534.5 MB  n=3   (28996, 768)      the embedding table
#              237.5 MB  n=8   (1, 128, 28996)   the one-hot intermediates
#              178.2 MB  n=1   (22268928,)       28996 x 768 flat
#              --------
#              950.2 MB = 41.5% of the peak, and every row of it is embedding-shaped.
# phase      75 s forward pass is a flat plateau:
#              run1   t+0s 2016 MB   t+30s 2008   t+70s 2077
#              run2   t+0s 2192      t+30s 2232   t+75s 2232
#            nothing retained past last use (s5_graph_clear_values 0.02%, also with pinned allocator).
# donor      SHAFT-GPU s2_embed_chunk (impl/embed_chunk_gpu.py; VRAM 2,406,400 -> 1,546,240 kB);
#            impl/levers/embed_chunk_cpu.py ports it with malloc_trim. N=16 = donor value.
# expected   -400 to -700 MB on 2,289,520 kB (-17% to -30%); spread 9.35%.
SHAFT_LEVERS=plaintext_free_cpu,triple_share_free_cpu,trace_nograd_cpu,onnx_single_file_export_cpu,encrypt_spill_cpu,embed_chunk_cpu
